Kotlin <code>build.gradle.kts</code>Groovy <code>build.gradle</code> <pre><code>unimined {
    minecraft {
        version = "1.7.10"
        patchBase("com.example:my-patches:1.0")
    }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>unimined {
    minecraft {
        version.set("1.7.10")
        patchBase("com.example:my-patches:1.0")
    }
}
</code></pre> <p>Resolves the dep onto the env's <code>patchBaseMain</code> configuration and applies its class patches to the environment's MC jar before remapping — compile classpath and dev runs both see the patched game. Patch entries are <code>.binpatch</code> (standard record) or <code>.bdiff</code> (PatchBase's checksum+gdiff unit); all other jar entries copy over verbatim.</p>

Kotlin <code>build.gradle.kts</code>Groovy <code>build.gradle</code> <pre><code>sourceSet("main") {
    patchBaseCreator()
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>sourceSet("main") {
    patchBaseCreator()
}
</code></pre> <p>Wires the loop tasks per environment (the full loop is walked through in Fork Development with Patch Sets):</p> Task Does <code>apply&lt;Env&gt;SourcePatch</code> applies <code>patches/</code> unified diffs onto the <code>gen&lt;Env&gt;Sources</code> output, writing only patch-covered files to <code>src/&lt;env&gt;/java</code> (generated — gitignore it) so compile + JarModAgent see patched sources. Skips when the patch dir doesn't exist <code>create&lt;Env&gt;SourcePatch</code> diffs <code>src/&lt;env&gt;/java</code> back into <code>patches/</code> — keeps the git-tracked patch source in sync. Skips when the overlay dir doesn't exist <code>create&lt;Env&gt;ClassPatch</code> diffs the <code>remap&lt;Env&gt;Jar</code> output vs <code>minecraftRaw</code> into the shippable patch jar (classifier <code>patch[-env]</code>) <code>recompile&lt;Env&gt;McClasses</code> compiles the overlay's <code>.java</code> files against the env's dev jar + Minecraft libraries <code>recompile&lt;Env&gt;Mc</code> merges the compiled classes + resource patches over the dev jar → a full dev-namespace Minecraft jar (classifier <code>recompiled</code>; the FG-era <code>recompMc</code> analog). Skips when the overlay doesn't exist <p>The <code>main</code> environment drops <code>&lt;Env&gt;</code> (<code>applySourcePatch</code>, <code>createSourcePatch</code>, <code>createClassPatch</code>, <code>recompileMc</code>, <code>recompileMcClasses</code>). The pre-2.0-convention names (<code>applySourcePatch&lt;Env&gt;</code>, <code>recompileMc&lt;Env&gt;</code>, …) still run — each is a deprecated alias that warns and delegates to the canonical task.</p> <p>Only <code>patches/</code> belongs in git. The generated patched sources and the built patch jar are artifacts.</p> <p>Warning</p> <p>Both source-patch tasks wipe and repopulate their output tree. <code>src/&lt;env&gt;/java</code> is the patch set's generated checkout — keep hand-written sources out of it, or retarget the overlay:</p> Kotlin <code>build.gradle.kts</code>Groovy <code>build.gradle</code> <pre><code>sourceSet("main") {
    patchBaseCreator {
        patchDir.set(layout.projectDirectory.dir("mc-patches"))
        sourceDir.set(layout.projectDirectory.dir("fork-src"))
        diffContextSize.set(5)      // hunk context lines (default 3)
        trimWhitespace.set(true)    // strip leading whitespace (default)
        patchFormat.set("bdiff")    // or "binpatch" (default)
    }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>sourceSet("main") {
    patchBaseCreator {
        patchDir.set(layout.projectDirectory.dir("mc-patches"))
        sourceDir.set(layout.projectDirectory.dir("fork-src"))
        diffContextSize.set(5)      // hunk context lines (default 3)
        trimWhitespace.set(true)    // strip leading whitespace (default)
        patchFormat.set("bdiff")    // or "binpatch" (default)
    }
}
</code></pre>

