</code></pre> Option Default Meaning <code>patchDir</code> <code>patches</code> (<code>patches/&lt;env&gt;</code>) git-tracked patch set — <code>*.patch</code> diffs + verbatim files <code>sourceDir</code> <code>src/&lt;env&gt;/java</code> generated overlay — wiped on apply/create <code>diffContextSize</code> <code>3</code> context lines in generated diffs <code>trimWhitespace</code> <code>true</code> strip leading whitespace when diffing <code>patchFormat</code> <code>binpatch</code> <code>createClassPatch</code> entry format — <code>binpatch</code> or <code>bdiff</code> <p>See adapters/patchbase for the consume-side DSL (<code>patchBase("g:a:v")</code>) and binding notes.</p>

Kotlin <code>build.gradle.kts</code>Groovy <code>build.gradle</code> <pre><code>uniminedPublish {
    javaPublication()                 // opt-in ordinary `java` component
    mavenPublications.set(false)      // opt out of all Maven publications
    environment("main") {
        groupId = "com.example"
        artifactId = "examplemod"
        version = "1.0.0"
    }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>uniminedPublish {
    javaPublication()                 // opt-in ordinary `java` component
    mavenPublications.set(false)      // opt out of all Maven publications
    environment("main") {
        groupId.set("com.example")
        artifactId.set("examplemod")
        version.set("1.0.0")
    }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>mavenPublications</code> is on by default: the host applies <code>maven-publish</code> and creates one <code>MavenPublication</code> per <code>unimined&lt;Env&gt;</code> component. Set it to <code>false</code> for component-only or ModPublisher-only builds — no publications are created at all (the <code>publishing { }</code> extension still exists for your own use). <code>javaPublication()</code> opts the ordinary <code>components.java</code> into a <code>java</code> publication — it only takes effect while <code>mavenPublications</code> is enabled, and defaults its artifactId to <code>&lt;project&gt;-java</code> since <code>uniminedMain</code> already claims <code>&lt;project&gt;</code>.</p>

Kotlin <code>build.gradle.kts</code>Groovy <code>build.gradle</code> <pre><code>unimined {
    runs {
        named("client") {           // creates if absent
            jvmArgs.add("-Xmx4G")
        }
        create("ciClient") {        // a custom variant
            prod.set(false)
        }
        runs.configureEach {        // every run
            environmentVariables.put("MC_DEBUG", "1")
        }
        configFirst("client") {     // applies before other config
            jvmArgs.add("-Xms1G")   // (declare it first)
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <pre><code>unimined {
    runs {
        named("client") {           // creates if absent
            jvmArgs.add("-Xmx4G")
        }
        create("ciClient") {        // a custom variant
            prod.set(false)
        }
        runs.configureEach {        // every run
            environmentVariables.put("MC_DEBUG", "1")
        }
        configFirst("client") {     // applies before other config
            jvmArgs.add("-Xms1G")   // (declare it first)
        }
    }
}
</code></pre> <p><code>configFirst</code> applies its action ahead of <code>named</code>/<code>create</code>/ <code>configureEach</code>/<code>all</code> configuration of the same run — the 1.x hook for laying down values later blocks can override (plugins use it for defaults). Declare it before other configuration of the run: a <code>configFirst</code> issued after the run already configured applies immediately — after whatever already ran.</p> <p>Tasks are <code>run&lt;Name&gt;</code> — <code>gradle runClient</code>, <code>runProdServer</code>, <code>runFabricData</code>, …</p>
